<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zadar</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Zara, Iader, Jadera</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zadar is a city on the Adriatic coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a>, known in Italian as Zara. A Roman colony as Iader, it was later a leading Dalmatian city contested between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a> sacked it for Venice in 1202. Ruled by Venice from 1409 to 1797, it then served as capital of the Austrian Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a>, and was held by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> from 1920 to 1947.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zadar.jpg" alt="Zadar" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: dronepicr · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roman_Forum_in_Zadar,_Croatia_(48607823862).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
